{
  "description": "Golden test vectors for the BRH constraint evaluation contract. The semantics of `op`/`value` against an observed runtime value is implemented twice \u2014 cobra/brh/contract.py (reference, used by tests and by MCP proxy) and cobra/http_proxy/brh_check.py (HTTP enforcer, stdlib-only) \u2014 with no runtime dependency between the two processes. Both test suites consume this file: any semantic divergence turns into a named red test on the diverging side. Update this file first when the contract evolves.",
  "semantics": [
    "Strict types, no coercion: a JSON string never equals a number ('42' != 42), mirroring pydantic Strict* in cobra/brh/schema.py.",
    "bool is not a number: although bool is a subclass of int in Python, True never satisfies a numeric constraint (== 1, <= 2, ...).",
    "Numeric cross-type comparison is allowed between int and float (42 == 42.0, 42 <= 42.99).",
    "String comparison is exact and case-sensitive.",
    "Unresolved placeholders ('trigger_value', 'from_plan') as constraint value make the constraint unsatisfiable - fail-closed, never a wildcard, even on a literal string match.",
    "Ordering ops (<=, >=) are numeric-only: a non-numeric constraint value or observed value is a violation.",
    "'in' membership uses the same typed equality as '=='; an empty set or a set containing a placeholder member is unsatisfiable.",
    "Unknown ops are unsatisfiable (fail-closed).",
    "null/None observed values never satisfy any constraint.",
    "Structural ops: 'eq_struct' pins a whole list/dict by recursive value equality (scalar leaves keep ==-strict typing); 'subset' requires every observed list element to value-match a planned member, blocking list-append attacks. Both are unsatisfiable if any placeholder remains in value."
  ],
  "vectors": [
    {
      "id": "le-int-vs-float-sat",
      "constraint": {
        "op": "<=",
        "value": 42.99
      },
      "observed": 42,
      "expect": "satisfied",
      "note": "int observed vs float constraint: numeric cross-type comparison"
    },
    {
      "id": "le-violation",
      "constraint": {
        "op": "<=",
        "value": 42.99
      },
      "observed": 500,
      "expect": "violation",
      "note": "the canonical branch-steering case: payload exceeds trigger_value"
    },
